---
// Page 05 — /snagging-dubai/cost/ · DOOR · Template B
// Format per spec: price table by unit size. No gate, no form above the fold.
import PageShell from '../../../layouts/PageShell.astro';
import DataTable from '../../../components/DataTable.astro';
import FaqList from '../../../components/FaqList.astro';
import ValuationCrossLink from '../../../components/ValuationCrossLink.astro';
import NeedsSource from '../../../components/NeedsSource.astro';
import { byPath } from '../../../lib/pages.js';

const page = byPath('/snagging-dubai/cost/');

const answer =
  'Snagging in Dubai costs AED 666–999 for a typical apartment, priced by unit size rather ' +
  'than by defect count. Studios sit below that band and villas above it. The fee most rate ' +
  'cards leave out is the re-inspection visit after the developer has completed the work, ' +
  'which is charged separately.';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How much does snagging cost in Dubai?',
    a:
      'AED 666–999 for a typical apartment. The price is driven by floor area and the number ' +
      'of systems to test, not by how many defects are found, so a badly built unit does not ' +
      'cost more to survey than a good one.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why do snagging quotes vary so much for the same apartment?',
    a:
      'Because "snagging" covers two different services. A visual walkthrough with a written ' +
      'list is cheap. An instrumented survey with thermal imaging, water pressure testing and ' +
      'electrical checks costs more and finds the defects that matter. Ask which one the quote ' +
      'is for.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is re-inspection included in the snagging fee?',
    a:
      'Usually not. Most Dubai firms price the first inspection and charge the return visit ' +
      'separately, and the return visit is where you confirm the developer actually fixed what ' +
      'was listed. Budget for both from the start.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does a bigger apartment cost more to snag?',
    a:
      'Yes. Pricing follows floor area and system count, so a three-bedroom unit costs more ' +
      'than a one-bedroom, and a villa more again because it adds a roof, external walls, ' +
      'drainage and often a pool.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is snagging worth AED 666–999 on a property already paid for?',
    a:
      'The comparison that matters is against the cost of the defects, not against the ' +
      'purchase price. A single missed waterproofing failure in a bathroom typically costs ' +
      'more to put right after the liability window closes than the survey did.',
  },
];
---

<PageShell page={page} h1="Snagging cost in Dubai, by unit size" answer={answer} faqs={faqs}>
  <h2>What does snagging cost by unit size?</h2>

  <DataTable
    caption="Dubai snagging prices by unit size, from published rate cards"
    columns={['Unit', 'Published price', 'What drives it']}
    rows={[
      [
        'Studio',
        '<span class="pending">[NEEDS SOURCE: published studio rate]</span>',
        'Smallest floor area, fewest systems',
      ],
      [
        '1–2 bed apartment',
        'AED 666–999',
        'The band most published Dubai rate cards sit inside',
      ],
      [
        '3+ bed apartment',
        '<span class="pending">[NEEDS SOURCE: published rate, 3-bed and above]</span>',
        'Floor area and additional wet rooms',
      ],
      [
        'Townhouse',
        '<span class="pending">[NEEDS SOURCE: published townhouse rate]</span>',
        'Adds external envelope and private drainage',
      ],
      [
        'Villa, up to 5 bed',
        '<span class="pending">[NEEDS SOURCE: published villa rate by bedroom count]</span>',
        'Roof, garden, pool plant, larger MEP load',
      ],
      [
        'Re-inspection visit',
        '<span class="pending">[NEEDS SOURCE: published re-inspection fee]</span>',
        'Charged separately by most firms',
      ],
    ]}
    source="Published Dubai snagging rate cards"
  />

  <p>
    Only the apartment band is filled because it is the only figure sourced to a published
    rate. The rest are marked rather than estimated, and this page does not ship to production
    until they are resolved against operators’ own published prices:{' '}
    <NeedsSource what="published rate cards from 8–10 named Dubai snagging operators, by unit size" />
  </p>

  <h2>Why is the re-inspection fee the one that surprises people?</h2>

  <p>
    Because the first inspection is what gets quoted and the second is what gets invoiced. The
    process only works if someone checks the developer’s remedial work, and that is a separate
    visit with a separate fee. An owner budgeting for one survey has budgeted for half the job.
  </p>

  <p>
    Firms that do publish a re-inspection price are, in practice, the ones expecting you to use
    it. A firm that will not quote the return visit up front is worth asking why.
  </p>

  <h2>What is included at that price, and what is not?</h2>

  <p>Typically included:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>The physical inspection of the unit against a standard defect list</li>
    <li>A written report with photographs, locations and severity</li>
    <li>A copy in a format you can forward to the developer</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Frequently not included, and worth confirming before you book:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>The re-inspection visit after remedial work</li>
    <li>Thermal imaging, where the firm treats it as an add-on</li>
    <li>Attendance at a meeting with the developer</li>
    <li>Any follow-up correspondence chasing the defect list</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How does this compare with what the defects cost?</h2>

  <p>
    That is the comparison to make, and it is the reason the survey is not really a cost
    decision. Within the developer’s one-year defect liability window, listed defects are
    remedied at their expense. Outside it, the same work is yours to pay for. The survey buys
    you the evidence and the timing;{' '}
    <a href="/snagging-dubai/developer-defect-liability/">the defect liability window</a>{' '}
    explains what expires when.
  </p>

  <p>
    What an inspection covers point by point is on{' '}
    <a href="/snagging-dubai/checklist/">the Dubai snagging checklist</a>, and{' '}
    <a href="/snagging-dubai/">snagging in Dubai</a> covers how the whole process sequences.
  </p>

  <ValuationCrossLink
    before="If the snag list turns out worse than expected and you are reconsidering the purchase, "
    anchor="a current valuation of the unit"
    after=" is the first number you need."
  />

  <FaqList faqs={faqs} />
</PageShell>
